    "Color scheme: auto (light). Switch to light": "crwdns117691:0crwdne117691:0",
    "Link to this heading": "crwdns117693:0crwdne117693:0",
    "Thank you for considering contributing to our open source project! We welcome all contributions, whether you’re fixing\na bug, improving documentation, or adding a new feature.": "crwdns117695:0crwdne117695:0",
    "Before you start, please take a moment to read our code of conduct and community guidelines, which outline our\nexpectations for respectful and inclusive behavior.": "crwdns117697:0crwdne117697:0",
    "Fork the repository on GitHub to create a copy of the project.": "crwdns117699:0crwdne117699:0",
    "Create a new branch for your changes. This will help if you need to create multiple pull requests, which may be\nout of scope from each other.": "crwdns117701:0crwdne117701:0",
    "Make your changes, be sure to follow our code style guidelines and test your code thoroughly.": "crwdns117703:0crwdne117703:0",
    "Document your code changes to the best of your ability. This will help other contributors understand the\npurpose and functionality of your changes.": "crwdns117705:0crwdne117705:0",
    "You can also add missing documentation to any related code. Documentation is important for the maintainability\nof our projects.": "crwdns117707:0crwdne117707:0",
    "When you’re ready, submit a pull request using the template provided.": "crwdns117709:0crwdne117709:0",
    "To help us review your changes quickly and accurately, please follow these guidelines when submitting a pull request:": "crwdns117711:0crwdne117711:0",
    "Submit your pull request against the default branch. The pull request title should follow": "crwdns117713:0crwdne117713:0",
    "conventional commit": "crwdns117715:0crwdne117715:0",
    "guidelines. If we accept the PR, it will\nbe squashed and merged with the pull request title and number as the commit message.": "crwdns117717:0crwdne117717:0",
    "Complete the pull request template, including any relevant details about your changes and any associated issues.": "crwdns117719:0crwdne117719:0",
    "Use the official template, including when AI tools help write your PR description.": "crwdns117721:0crwdne117721:0",
    "Leave the template comments in place. They are helpful when editing the PR description.": "crwdns117723:0crwdne117723:0",
    "<!-- This is a comment -->": "crwdns117725:0crwdne117725:0",
    "Copy code": "crwdns117727:0crwdne117727:0",
    "Do not delete any sections of the template, even if they do not apply to your changes.": "crwdns117729:0crwdne117729:0",
    "Link any issues or discussions that are resolved by your changes.": "crwdns117731:0crwdne117731:0",
    "Closes #123": "crwdns117733:0crwdne117733:0",
    "Fixes #456": "crwdns117735:0crwdne117735:0",
    "Resolves #789": "crwdns117737:0crwdne117737:0",
    "Complete the checklists. It is not required to check everything, only check the items that apply to your changes.": "crwdns117739:0crwdne117739:0",
    "[x] This is a complete item": "crwdns117741:0crwdne117741:0",
    "[ ] This is an incomplete item": "crwdns117743:0crwdne117743:0",
    "Be prepared to address any feedback or questions that may arise during the code review process.": "crwdns117745:0crwdne117745:0",
    "Note": "crwdns117747:0crwdne117747:0",
    "It is important to note that pull requests should generally address a single issue or feature to make it\neasier to review and test the code. In some cases, exceptions may be made. For example, if you find a typo or\nformatting error in a file being modified, it may be acceptable to fix it in the same pull request as a drive-by\nfix. However, if the pull request is already large, it may be better to create a separate pull request for the\nsecondary fixes.": "crwdns117749:0crwdne117749:0",
    "Pull requests may be reviewed by project maintainers, AI agents, or both to ensure code quality and consistency with\nproject standards. AI agents help us keep up with the high volume of incoming pull requests. Maintainers remain\nresponsible for merge decisions.": "crwdns117751:0crwdne117751:0",
    "Address valid feedback from AI agents as you would feedback from a human reviewer. If a finding is incorrect or does\nnot apply, explain why with relevant code, tests, or other evidence. AI reviews can make mistakes, so use your\nengineering judgment when responding.": "crwdns117753:0crwdne117753:0",
    "The changes requested may be minor, such as fixing a typo, adjusting formatting, or adding a comment. These may seem\nlike small requests, but they are important to our projects as they help ensure that the code is readable,\nmaintainable, and consistent with the rest of the project. In other cases, the requested changes may be more\nsignificant. In either case, the maintainers will provide feedback to help you improve the code.": "crwdns117755:0crwdne117755:0",
    "Please keep in mind that partially complete pull requests will not be merged. Before merging, we will consider the\nfollowing criteria:": "crwdns117757:0crwdne117757:0",
    "Does the code follow the style guidelines of the project?": "crwdns117759:0crwdne117759:0",
    "Does the change add value?": "crwdns117761:0crwdne117761:0",
    "Is the code well commented?": "crwdns117763:0crwdne117763:0",
    "Have documentation blocks been updated for new or modified components?": "crwdns117765:0crwdne117765:0",
    "Will the changes create issues in other scenarios?": "crwdns117767:0crwdne117767:0",
    "Have appropriate tests, including regression tests, been added or updated?": "crwdns117769:0crwdne117769:0",
    "Developers and maintainers will attempt to assist with challenging issues.": "crwdns117771:0crwdne117771:0",
    "We enforce consistent code style across our projects to improve readability and maintainability of the codebase.\nHere are some of the guidelines we follow:": "crwdns117773:0crwdne117773:0",
    "Each file, with few exceptions, should end with an empty line.": "crwdns117775:0crwdne117775:0",
    "In most cases, the maximum line length should not exceed 120 characters to make the code more readable.": "crwdns117777:0crwdne117777:0",
    "We use": "crwdns117779:0crwdne117779:0",
    "yamllint": "crwdns117781:0crwdne117781:0",
    "to lint our": "crwdns117783:0crwdne117783:0",
    "yaml": "crwdns117785:0crwdne117785:0",
    "files. You can find the configuration file": "crwdns117787:0crwdne117787:0",
    "here": "crwdns117789:0crwdne117789:0",
    "in our": "crwdns117791:0crwdne117791:0",
    ".github": "crwdns117793:0crwdne117793:0",
    "repository.": "crwdns117795:0crwdne117795:0",
    "CodeQL": "crwdns117797:0crwdne117797:0",
    "and": "crwdns117799:0crwdne117799:0",
    "SonarCloud": "crwdns117801:0crwdne117801:0",
    "to analyze our codebases.\nThere will be a comment on your PR indicating if there are any issues that need to be addressed.\nPlease address these issues if reasonable.\nIn some cases, there may be false positives, use your best judgment to determine if changes should be made.\nThese tools are not perfect and not meant to override engineering judgment.": "crwdns117803:0crwdne117803:0",
    "Want to address SonarCloud issues locally before committing?\nYou can use the": "crwdns117805:0crwdne117805:0",
    "SonarLint": "crwdns117807:0crwdne117807:0",
    "plugin for your IDE.": "crwdns117809:0crwdne117809:0",
    "AI tools and agents are welcome for brainstorming, implementation, debugging, refactoring, testing, documentation,\nand preparing PR descriptions. This includes substantial AI-assisted changes, provided they meet the same quality\nstandards as any other contribution.": "crwdns117811:0crwdne117811:0",
    "You are responsible for all contributions submitted under your name, including work produced by an AI agent.\nBefore submitting a PR:": "crwdns117813:0crwdne117813:0",
    "Review the full diff and understand how the changes work. Be prepared to explain your implementation and decisions.": "crwdns117815:0crwdne117815:0",
    "Verify the accuracy of generated code, documentation, and PR descriptions. Remove errors, invented claims, and\nunrelated changes.": "crwdns117817:0crwdne117817:0",
    "Follow the project’s established patterns, conventions, and contribution guidelines.": "crwdns117819:0crwdne117819:0",
    "Test the changes and add appropriate automated coverage, including regression tests as described below.": "crwdns117821:0crwdne117821:0",
    "Report the validation you actually performed and any limitations, such as tests you could not run.": "crwdns117823:0crwdne117823:0",
    "Contributions that contain errors, do not solve the stated problem, or fail to meet our quality standards may be\nrejected regardless of how they were created.": "crwdns117825:0crwdne117825:0",
    "Check the box in the PR template’s AI Usage section if AI tools were used while preparing the PR. Leave it unchecked\nif no AI tools were used. You may optionally describe how AI helped.": "crwdns117827:0crwdne117827:0",
    "Our": "crwdns117829:0crwdne117829:0",
    "community rules": "crwdns117831:0crwdne117831:0",
    "prohibit AI-generated issues and posts. Use the standard issue template and describe the issue in your own words.": "crwdns117833:0crwdne117833:0",
    "Testing is a critical part of our development process, and we have automated tests and tools to ensure that our code\nmeets the expected quality and functionality.": "crwdns117835:0crwdne117835:0",
    "To ensure consistent code style, we run automated tests on pull requests. The tests that run depend on the language(s)\nof the repository. The following table shows the labels and the corresponding tests that will run:": "crwdns117837:0crwdne117837:0",
