    "shellcheck": "crwdns117875:0crwdne117875:0",
    "Projects may have additional checks,": "crwdns117877:0crwdne117877:0",
    "eslint": "crwdns117879:0crwdne117879:0",
    "for example, depending on the project’s requirements.": "crwdns117881:0crwdne117881:0",
    "We strive to have comprehensive unit tests for our projects, but this is still a work in progress for some projects.\nWe welcome contributions that improve test coverage and add new tests.": "crwdns117883:0crwdne117883:0",
    "Automated tests, including regression tests, are expected for most code changes. For bug fixes, add a regression test\nthat reproduces the original issue, fails without the fix, and passes with it. For new or modified functionality,\ncover the intended behavior and relevant edge cases. Follow the project’s existing test framework and conventions.\nPRs should not drastically reduce coverage percentages.": "crwdns117885:0crwdne117885:0",
    "Documentation-only changes and other changes without testable behavior may not need automated tests. If automated\ntesting is impractical for your change, explain why in the PR and describe the manual validation you performed.\nInclude the test commands and results in the PR’s Testing section, along with any checks you could not run.": "crwdns117887:0crwdne117887:0",
    "Please reach out if you would like assistance writing tests.": "crwdns117889:0crwdne117889:0",
    "All Python projects in the LizardByte organization use": "crwdns117891:0crwdne117891:0",
    "uv": "crwdns117893:0crwdne117893:0",
    "for dependency management,\nPython environment setup, lock files, and command execution. A Python project’s": "crwdns117895:0crwdne117895:0",
    "pyproject.toml": "crwdns117897:0crwdne117897:0",
    "uv.lock": "crwdns117899:0crwdne117899:0",
    "files\nare the source of truth for its dependencies.": "crwdns117901:0crwdne117901:0",
    "Use the Python version declared by the project instead of assuming the same version across every repository. After\nchanging Python dependencies or project metadata, update and commit the lock file with the related change.": "crwdns117903:0crwdne117903:0",
    "Common uv commands:": "crwdns117905:0crwdne117905:0",
    "uv lock --check\nuv": "crwdns117907:0crwdne117907:0",
    "sync": "crwdns117909:0crwdne117909:0",
    "--frozen\nuv run --locked python -m pytest\nuv lock": "crwdns117911:0crwdne117911:0",
    "Useful tips:": "crwdns117913:0crwdne117913:0",
    "Use": "crwdns117915:0crwdne117915:0",
    "lock": "crwdns117917:0crwdne117917:0",
    "--check": "crwdns117919:0crwdne117919:0",
    "in validation to confirm the lock file still matches": "crwdns117921:0crwdne117921:0",
    "--frozen": "crwdns117923:0crwdne117923:0",
    "in custom build or CI commands to install only from": "crwdns117925:0crwdne117925:0",
    "without updating it.": "crwdns117927:0crwdne117927:0",
    "Use native uv integrations for hosted services when available, and add a lockfile drift check when they cannot pass": "crwdns117929:0crwdne117929:0",
    "directly.": "crwdns117931:0crwdne117931:0",
    "run": "crwdns117933:0crwdne117933:0",
    "--locked": "crwdns117935:0crwdne117935:0",
    "<command>": "crwdns117937:0crwdne117937:0",
    "when you want to run a project command without changing": "crwdns117939:0crwdne117939:0",
    "locally when you want uv to fail if": "crwdns117941:0crwdne117941:0",
    "is missing or out of date.": "crwdns117943:0crwdne117943:0",
    "only when dependency inputs changed and the lock file should be updated.": "crwdns117945:0crwdne117945:0",
    "Prefer project-specific commands from each repository’s documentation when they exist.": "crwdns117947:0crwdne117947:0",
    "LizardByte projects are used by people all over the world. When feasible, we strive to make our projects\nmultilingual. If you are able to contribute translations, we would be grateful for your help.": "crwdns117949:0crwdne117949:0",
    "The translations occur on": "crwdns117951:0crwdne117951:0",
    ".\nAnyone is free to contribute to the localization there. The project on CrowdIn is a mono-project, meaning that all\ntranslations are done in one place. This allows for easier management of translations across projects.": "crwdns117953:0crwdne117953:0",
    "Translation Basics": "crwdns117955:0crwdne117955:0",
    "The brand name": "crwdns117957:0crwdne117957:0",
    "and project names should never be translated.": "crwdns117959:0crwdne117959:0",
    "Other brand names should never be translated. Examples include": "crwdns117961:0crwdne117961:0",
    "AMD": "crwdns117963:0crwdne117963:0",
    "Intel": "crwdns117965:0crwdne117965:0",
    ", and": "crwdns117967:0crwdne117967:0",
    "NVIDIA": "crwdns117969:0crwdne117969:0",
    "CrowdIn Integration": "crwdns117971:0crwdne117971:0",
    "How does it work?": "crwdns117973:0crwdne117973:0",
    "When a change is made to a project’s source code, CrowdIn will automatically receive the updated strings.": "crwdns117975:0crwdne117975:0",
    "Once translations are updated on CrowdIn, a push gets made to the": "crwdns117977:0crwdne117977:0",
    "l10n_master": "crwdns117979:0crwdne117979:0",
    "branch and a PR is made against the": "crwdns117981:0crwdne117981:0",
    "master": "crwdns117983:0crwdne117983:0",
    "branch. Once the PR is merged, all updated translations are part of the project and will be included in the\nnext release.": "crwdns117985:0crwdne117985:0",
    "The extraction process varies by project. Please consult the project’s documentation for more information.": "crwdns117987:0crwdne117987:0",
    "Thank you to all the contributors who have helped with translations. Your contributions are greatly appreciated!": "crwdns117989:0crwdne117989:0",
    "We require that all contributors sign a Contributor License Agreement (CLA) before we can merge their pull requests.\nIf any action is required, a bot will comment on your PR with instructions.\nExempt repositories are listed below.": "crwdns117991:0crwdne117991:0",
